on\n</paths>\n<description>\nComplete partial paths inside a framed rectangle by projecting external color traces inward.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg, a 1px rectangular frame (border color) with uniform interior fill.\n- Colored components outside the frame touching its edges.\n\nRule:\n- Output = the frame's interior, filled with the fill color.\n- Map each outside component's frame-touch points into interior coordinates.\n- Monochrome components become solid Manhattan stripes between mapped endpoints.\n- Two-color components become alternating-color Manhattan paths.\n\nKey insight: Endpoint colors of two-color traces anchor the alternating phase deterministically.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"touch point s on closed rectangular frame where an open rectangular frame touches it\",\n  \"dst\": \"connect to another touch point d on closed rectangular frame where an open rectangular frame touches it\",\n  \"path\": \"path to complete the open rectangular frame\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"same color and pattern as the open rectangular frame\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"crop to only retain inner area of the closed rectangular frame\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"278e5215\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3627\nmechanism=0.4035\nlexical=0.0129\ncode_feature=0.7143\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, code:counter, code:output_resize, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:crop_resize, operation:recolor, operation:translate, output:crop, relation:inside\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/278e5215.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/278e5215.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nRecolor the large mask crop column-by-column using the separate three-row palette strip.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the most common color.\n- One large monochrome foreground object is the mask; its bbox is the output region and may contain background holes.\n- The remaining foreground is a 3-row palette rectangle with the same width as the mask bbox: two identical color rows and one uniform row.\n\nRule:\n- Crop to the mask object's bbox.\n- For each output column, color mask pixels with the corresponding color from the repeated palette rows.\n- Replace background holes inside the crop with the palette's uniform third-row color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe grey object is only a stencil; its columns select colors from the legend, while its holes expose the legend's fill color.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"palette column s in the separate 3-row strip\",\n  \"dst\": \"column d in the mask bbox crop\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"s.column == d.column_in_crop\",\n  \"transform\": \"recolor mask pixels in d with s.repeated_row_color; fill background holes with the palette's uniform third-row color\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"3-row palette strip maps each mask-crop column to its mask color; the uniform third row gives the hole color\",\n  \"grid_shape\": \"crop to mask bbox\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"9385bd28\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3538\nmechanism=0.4508\nlexical=0.0114\ncode_feature=0.3750\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:counter, code:output_resize, object:marker, object:rectangle, object:sprite, operation:count, operation:flood_fill, operation:recolor, operation:sort_order, operation:translate, relation:adjacent, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:overlap\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/9385bd28.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/9385bd28.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill rectangles between diagonal marker pairs using a color legend.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg grid with a vertical legend at the bottom-left: each row is a (marker_color, fill_color) pair.\n- Scattered L-shaped corner markers