 non-bg non-marker colors found; cannot determine wall color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8e5c0c38/D5/0/code.py:66:      the marker color from sprite processing and erase it in the output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8e5c0c38/D5/0/code.py:145:    - bg is the dominant background color. Red (2) is a special marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/898e7135/6/code.py:241:    - Tight-crop the hole layout inside the frame and read each slot's marker color from the wall pixels touching that hole.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D14/0/code.py:207:    assert other_cols, \"no non-bg non-marker colors found; cannot determine wall color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/36/code.py:29:#   and equal marker colors define the pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/36/code.py:50:#   present, and repeated marker colors on paired frame corners / nested sprite corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/36/code.py:87:# - Every frame and sprite has its marker at `[0, 0]` and marker colors are unique per pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/36/code.py:100:# marker colors; this prevents tight-grid frames from merging through neighbor markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/36/code.py:150:      square; matched pairs share that marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/36/code.py:155:    - Pair a frame with the sprite whose top-left marker color is the same.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/36/code.py:161:    - The reliable cue is the repeated marker color at a fixed semantic location, not the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8e5c0c38/D2/3/code.py:22:      - Red (2) is reserved as an external marker color and never used by sprites or bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8e5c0c38/D2/3/code.py:141:    - bg is the most common color. Red (2) is a detached marker color, not part of the sprite payload.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6ffbe589/24/code.py:71:# - No new marker colors are introduced; cues keep the same-color matching relation from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D14/1/code.py:40:#   - `wall_col = most frequent non-bg non-marker color` 依赖“墙只有一种颜色”。变体下若仍这样做，\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/23/code.py:125:    - Every ordinary frame border uses the same visible color. Frames that were originally invisible are shown instead with one special marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8698868d/23/code.py:444:#   minority marker color. The generator guarantees at least one of each and ensures\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/10/code.py:174:    - One background color fills most cells. Red (2) is a special marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/19/code.py:36:#       The sprite carries the same marker colors at the same relative offsets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/19/code.py:80:#    - marker color(s) inside the empty slot,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6ffbe589/3/code.py:61:    - No hidden use of color ids, ordering, or extra marker colors is introduced.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/5/code.py:134:    - Outside the strip are full rectangular sprites, each carrying one connector pixel of a matching marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/5/code.py:143:    - Duplicate rectangle sizes are intentional. The correct match is not determined by size alone, nor by marker color alone:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5dbc8537/5/code.py:144:      the sprite's connector pixel must match both the slot's marker color and its exact relative position inside the rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e376de54/7/code.py:175:    - Within that target interval, cells that belonged to the input segment stay in the segment's original color, cells needed only to extend a short segment become marker color 4, and any cells