ors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/1/code.py:155:    - Non-marker colors appear as one-cell-thick horizontal/vertical line fragments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/1/code.py:172:    assert colors, \"expected foreground line and marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D5/1/code.py:183:    assert marker_colors, \"expected singleton marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:32:# - Template colors are sampled without repetition, and marker colors are chosen\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/10/code.py:64:#   scanning, so the template rule has a real effect once the marker color fixes the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/8/code.py:17:#   the ordered pair of marker colors to orient it so marker 5 is at the output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/8/code.py:37:#   rectangular, its two unique marker colors sit on the same edge, and the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/8/code.py:317:    assert set(pos) == {MARKER_TL, MARKER_TR}, \"anchor must contain exactly the two marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/3/code.py:88:    - Interior sprites are multi-color connected components; each has a rare marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/3/code.py:92:    - Pair each sprite with the border segment whose color matches the sprite marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/21/code.py:354:    assert len(set(colors)) >= 2, \"marker colors must expose multiple cycle phases\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D9/1/code.py:317:    - Non-marker colors form thin horizontal/vertical stroke fragments that may now include same-color T or + junctions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D9/1/code.py:334:    assert colors, \"expected foreground line and marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D9/1/code.py:345:    assert marker_colors, \"expected singleton marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:28:#      repeated marker color per grid and splits that color across both anchors of its pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:47:#    - A human can see two same-color border anchors and infer that identical marker colors may\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:69:    - Each marker color appears as two isolated border anchors on opposite edges.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:72:    - Match each sprite to the two border anchors sharing its marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D4/2/code.py:163:        # --- STEP 3) Decide marker color for this component. ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/4/code.py:170:        assert launch is not None, f\"marker color {int(v)} must have a direction mapping\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/4/code.py:245:    Simulate border markers whose launch direction is encoded by marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D1/1/code.py:105:    - Non-marker colors form one-cell-thick horizontal/vertical stroke fragments that may overlap at crossings.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D1/1/code.py:122:    assert colors, \"expected foreground line and marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D1/1/code.py:133:    assert marker_colors, \"expected singleton marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/17/code.py:173:    assert len(cols) == 1, \"each generated piece must use exactly one non-marker color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D1/2/code.py:106:    - Non-marker colors form one-cell-thick axis-aligned stroke fragments that may cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D1/2/code.py:123:    assert colors, \"expected foreground line and marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D1/2/code.py:134:    assert marker_colors, \"expected sin