ieces by marker color ascending; this fixes their output corner order:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/2/code.py:335:    - The same visible marker color carries two instructions at once: it says which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:20:#     objects: 1-cell-thick rectilinear polylines of 3-4 non-marker colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:214:    assert colors, \"expected foreground line and marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:223:    assert marker_colors <= KNOWN_MARKERS, f\"unexpected marker colors: {marker_colors}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/0/code.py:226:    assert marker_colors, \"expected singleton marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D15/1/code.py:66:    - The border contains one non-corner anchor pixel for each marker color; those anchor pixels may touch other non-background border decorations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D15/1/code.py:70:    - For each movable interior component, use its marker color to find the border pixel of the same color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D15/1/code.py:75:    - Isolation is no longer the signal for anchors. The stable cue is that marker colors point to unique border pixels, and the edge containing that border pixel determines the slide axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D15/1/code.py:90:    # --- STEP 1) Read candidate marker colors from interior multi-color sprites. ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/16/code.py:69:#      body color plus connector/marker colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/36/code.py:161:    - Azure squares are still processed by increasing input column and stacked on the left; red squares are processed by decreasing input column and stacked on the right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/1/code.py:40:#   marker colors and asserts that each marker component is 