Decide marker color for this component. ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/2/code.py:75:    Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network by reinterpreting one shared marker color as either a missing bend cell or an arm-side redirection control.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/2/code.py:90:    Key insight: The marker color no longer tells you its job. The local geometry does: embedded bend markers restore missing corners, while offset single-neighbor markers flip an arm and force a new boundary-reaching ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/2/code.py:97:    assert colors, \"expected foreground line and marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D3/2/code.py:108:    assert marker_colors, \"expected singleton marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/23/code.py:204:    - Azure squares are processed by increasing input column and placed toward the left side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/10/code.py:28:#   8-connected components, detects per-component singleton marker colors, sorts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/10/code.py:343:    - Extract the four connected pieces and sort them by marker color: 5 first, then 6, then 8, and finally the unmarked piece.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/10/code.py:349:    - The singleton marker colors no longer just identify an anchor; together they encode the assembly sequence, and the absence of a marker encodes the \"do not rotate\" exception.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:26:#      one marker color from the region and says \"start the boundary band with this\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:361:    - One wall cell next to each region is recolored as a clue dot; that dot repeats one marker color from the adjacent region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:364:    - Recover the true wall mask structurally, then for each region sort its internal marker colors by boundary distance and prepend the base color if the first marker starts deeper than distance 0.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/18/code.py:390:# ---- Distinct marker colors across the whole grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/19/code.py:34:#      anchor uses a marker color.  This variant extracts 8-connected pieces.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7b3084d4/19/code.py:57:#    - Exactly one piece contains the singleton marker color 5.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/0/code.py:428:    - Any color whose 4-connected components are all singletons is a marker color rather than a line color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/0/code.py:444:    assert colors, \"expected foreground line and marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D12/0/code.py:455:    assert marker_colors, \"expected singleton marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:20:#       deepest marker color C, so the solver can infer both spiral start/direction and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:316:    - The same corner also has a short inward diagonal of distinct marker colors, ordered from shallow to deeper Chebyshev depths.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/25/code.py:320:    - Read the diagonal marker colors by increasing depth, reverse that list, then append the region base color to complete the repeating palette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D13/1/code.py:49:#    flag. The same marker color appears in both partitions, so a human solver can\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D13/1/code.py:61:    Slide interior sprites toward the border anchor that matches both their marker color and their background partition.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D13/1/code.py:70:    - Match a sprite to the anchor of the same marker color inside that same region.\n/home/li