r color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/24/code.py:228:    - Inside the chosen region, order marker colors by boundary distance to form the palette, prepending the base color if the shallowest marker is not on the boundary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/24/code.py:259:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D4/0/code.py:147:    - Non-marker colors form one-cell-thick horizontal/vertical polyline fragments that may cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D4/0/code.py:165:    assert colors, \"expected foreground line and marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D4/0/code.py:176:    assert marker_colors, \"expected singleton marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/1/code.py:70:#   - Distinct marker colors within a region stay few and ordered by visible path\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/0/code.py:83:    - Match each sprite to the anchor sharing its marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/27/code.py:44:#      one border marker color).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/27/code.py:61:#    - Crop colors are sampled from 1..9 while board/border marker color is 0,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/27/code.py:80:#    - The output uses a fixed border marker color that never appears inside the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:36:#       - color every displayed dot with the same fixed marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:61:#       component in the input. The fixed marker color only appears in output.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:75:#       the solver writes a fixed marker color that is independent of frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:76:#       color. The generator reserves this marker color so it is distinct from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:94:#     positive tallies using the same marker color in the same sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:104:#   - A single fixed marker color is easier to infer than a many-to-many color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:107:#   - Reserving the marker color away from every input object prevents false\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:108:#     cues such as distractors sharing the output marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:120:#   - The intended marker color is globally fixed rather than frame-dependent.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:205:    - Use one fixed marker color for all frames instead of reusing each frame's border color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8f215267/25/code.py:209:      the quantity is inverted, the placement direction is mirrored, and the marker color is globally shared.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/2/code.py:17:#   If that quadrant matches the marked corner, transfer the source marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/2/code.py:28:#   at least one destination receives a marker color and at least one receives a center color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/2/code.py:387:      - marker color in exactly one corner cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D3/2/code.py:479:    - Compare destination position to that source: if the destination lies in the marker corner's quadrant, copy the marker color; otherwise copy the source center color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D6/0/code.py:104:    assert colors, \"expected foreground line and marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/faa9f03d/D6/0/code.py:115:    assert marker_colors, \"expected singleton marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/1/code.py:18:#      whose least-frequent color is the marker. Matching is still by marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/1/code.py:21:#      wide continuous line in the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/1/code.py:26:#        (5,2),(5,3),(5,4),(5,5),(5,6) with the marker color. The anchor stays on the border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/1/code.py:29:#    - Use the marker color itself as the trail color. This avoids introducing a second color mapping\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/1/code.py:56:#    - Samples still mix multiple sprites and repeated marker colors, so the solver must infer the axis\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/1/code.py:64:#    - Trail color = marker color, which is directly visible in both input sprite and border anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/1/code.py:95:    - Isolated non-bg border pixels act as anchors, and the anchor color matches the sprite marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/1/code.py:98:    - Match each sprite to the anchor with the same marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D6/1/code.py:100:    - After removing the source sprite, redraw the marker's traversed cells as a continuous trail in the marker color, while keeping the anchor unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/7/code.py:19:#   region had marker colors A/B/C at boundary depths 0/1/2, output rings were\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/7/code.py:174:      treat it as radius 0. Order the marker colors by their Chebyshev radius from\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/7/code.py:229:# ---- Distinct marker colors across grid ----\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:17:#     and each active marker color is still realized as a diagonal pair of L-corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9385bd28/18/code.py:26:#   - Example: suppose a marker color forms L anchors at TL=(2,4) and BR=(6,9).\n/home/