 The generator rejects cases where ignoring marker colors would yield the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/10/code.py:354:        f\"unexpected marker colors {set(markers.values()) - ACTIVE_COLORS}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/10/code.py:376:            f\"landed on marker color {landed_color}, expected current color {current_color}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/10/code.py:438:    variable telling you which visible marker color is currently edible and which color will become active next.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/5/code.py:226:    # --- STEP 2) Identify the blob body color and unique port-marker color. ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/11/code.py:96:    - Non-marker colors appear only as one-cell-thick horizontal or vertical\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/11/code.py:125:    assert colors, \"expected foreground line and marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/11/code.py:136:    assert marker_colors, \"expected singleton marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D8/0/code.py:36:#     - Suppose marker color A has TL+BR L-corners. Original logic: fill the TR-BL rectangle in the legend's fill\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D8/0/code.py:160:    - Outside the legend, each referenced marker color appears either as two opposite L-corners or as a solid 2x2 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D8/0/code.py:164:    - Read the legend from bottom to top and gather the non-legend pixels of each marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/19/code.py:265:    assert len(marker_hits) == 1, f\"expected exactly 1 marker color, got report={report}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/7/code.py:212:    assert colors, \"expected foreground line and marker colors\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/faa9f03d/7/code.py:221:    assert marker_colors <= KNOWN_MA