ithout a companion, paint every beat cell across the whole line in the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D3/2/code.py:19:#    - The old task used one paint color per active line: either the marker color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D3/2/code.py:30:#      old output on beats 0,2,4,6,8 was all marker color; new output becomes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D3/2/code.py:51:#    - Every line still contains exactly one repeated marker color with exactly two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D3/2/code.py:99:    - Each active shooting-direction line has exactly one repeated marker color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/1/code.py:50:#    readable from the aligned endpoint itself; the preserved marker color is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/17/code.py:14:    2. Unmatched sprites no longer disappear. They become a dedicated marker color, pink.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/17/code.py:29:  - The marker color is outside the gradient palette, so the three output categories remain visually separable:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/17/code.py:154:LEGEND_COLORS = [1, 2, 3, 4, 7, 8, 9]  # marker color 6 is reserved away from legends\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/17/code.py:176:      Otherwise recolor the whole sprite with the dedicated marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/17/code.py:685:    \"\"\"Generate and place all sprites, painting expected output with gradient or marker colors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:16:#    one marker color to one fill color, but that marker color now appears in 2-3 separate L-pairs\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:30:#    The original code assumes all pixels of one marker color belong to one global bbox; that fails\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:43:#    which colors have 2 versus 3 pairs, so the \"same marker color applies multiple times\" pattern is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:52:#    to several repeated geometric instances of the same marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:233:    \"\"\"Split one marker color into L-corner components and recover the unique minimum-area perfect matching.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:246:    assert n % 2 == 0 and n >= 2, \"each marker color must have an even positive number of L-corners\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:298:    - Each legend row gives one marker color and its fill color, read from bottom to top.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:299:    - Outside the legend, every legend marker color appears as 2-3 separate L-pairs, each pair made of two disconnected 3-cell corner marks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/0/code.py:302:    - For each legend entry, gather all non-legend pixels of that marker color and split them into 3-cell L-corner components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D17/0/code.py:16:#   Each active row/column still has one repeated marker color with two dots:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D17/0/code.py:47:#   Colors still act locally: marker color fills when unobstructed, companion\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D17/0/code.py:75:      marker color with two dots: one on the shooting edge and one farther in.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D17/0/code.py:88:      With no such event, the marker color fills the whole line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/3/code.py:45:#    Generator lines still contain exactly one repeated marker color with two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/3/code.py:94:    - If there is no aligned absorber, the marker color fills the entire line\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/3/code.py:144:            f\"Line {li} ({'row' if by_row else 'col'}) must have exactly one repeated marker color: \"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b9e38dc0/D4/3/code.py:74:    - Flood the interior with the marker color and continue radiating through the opening; obstacles keep their colors and cast shadows behind them.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D17/1/code.py:23:#    - Example on a left-shooting row: marker color 2 at positions 0 and 3 gives\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D17/1/code.py:72:#    - The solver assumes each active line has exactly one marker color with exactly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D17/1/code.py:87:    - Every active shooting line has exactly one repeated marker color with exactly two dots;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D17/1/code.py:100:    - If there is no companion, fill the entire line's beat positions with the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/1/code.py:18:      - collect all pixels of one marker color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/1/code.py:125:    - For each active legend entry, the matching marker color appears exactly three times outside the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D14/1/code.py:129:    - Read legend entries from bottom to top and gather the non-legend pixels of that marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/2/code.py:7:#   Each active row/column still contains exactly one repeating marker color with\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/2/code.py:11:#   marker color. Small trace:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/2/code.py:25:#   the companion position must be detected and overwritten with the marker color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/2/code.py:37:#   endpoint changes back to marker color. That difference is directly visible in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/2/code.py:79:      marker color; bystanders are not changed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D7/2/code.py:83:    ray, lends its color to the track, and receives the marker color in return.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:18:#       The left cell is the output color; the right cell is the marker color to look for around sprite holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:37:#       hole rims and unique marker colors in the legend.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:44:#       marker color hugging holes inside sprites. The marker sits exactly where the legend says to look.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:183:        assert marker not in mapping, \"legend marker colors must be unique\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:216:    - In every pair, the left cell gives the target output color and the right cell gives the marker color to match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:217:    - Interior sprites are connected blobs made of grey plus one marker color painted on cells that touch enclosed holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e3721c99/39/code.py:488:    \"\"\"Recolor all hole-adjacent sprite cells with the marker color.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D12/2/code.py:8:#      either fill the full beat with the marker color, or fill one bounded span\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D12/2/code.py:44:#      cells that are still bg or the original marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D12/2/code.py:113:        f\"marker color: {dict(colors)}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D12/2/code.py:140:            f\"Line {line} ({'row' if by_row else 'col'}) non-marker color {col} \"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:9:#    - The non-legend area now contains several disconnected objects of that single marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:20:#        Therefore the new solver must split the marker color into connected components first,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:26:#    - All objects share one marker color and one fill color; this is the visible signature of D10.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:30:#    - `for ... in entries` previously assumed one marker color per object family. With one legend row,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:53:#    - Because the same marker color is reused across multiple objects, a solver can infer that the legend\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:211:    - The bottom-left legend is exactly one 2-cell row: marker color in the left cell, fill color in the right cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:212:    - Outside the legend, the same marker color appears in several disconnected objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:217:    - Split all non-legend pixels of that marker color into small connected pieces.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/0/code.py:296:# 3. All non-legend marker objects share the legend marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D4/3/code.py:46:#      but the generator must ensure at most one aligned non-marker color per line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D4/3/code.py:52:#   grouped marker color and at most one extra single pixel. The bars are isolated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D4/3/code.py:85:    - Each active line contains exactly one repeating marker color, represented by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D4/3/code.py:93:    - On each active line, detect the unique marker color by its two equal runs:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16de56c4/D4/3/code.py:101:      marker color. With a companion, also recolor both marker bars to the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:14:#     - Each legend row is (marker color, fill color), read bottom -> top.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:26:#       - The solver still reads those rows bottom -> top and processes each marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:35:#     - Using 6-8 entries is already near the ARC palette limit because marker colors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:44:#     - main() groups all non-legend pixels of one marker color into one object. Therefore\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:45:#       each legend marker color must correspond to exactly one placed marker group or be\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:49:#     - main() protects future marker colors by legend order. With 6-8 rows this becomes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:166:    - Each legend row stores a marker color in the left cell and its fill color in the right cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:167:    - Elsewhere, each marker color appears either as one diagonal pair of L-corners or as one solid 2x2 block.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:171:    - For an L-pair, collect that marker color's non-legend pixels, find which diagonal holds the L-anchors,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D10/1/code.py:387:    \"\"\"Create the legend grid, rows, mask, and marker colors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/14/code.py:37:#     mover's marker color. This is strong enough to see, but not so unconstrained that examples\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/14/code.py:44:#     Fix: collect row/col marks by marker color, then translate marker -> sprite main color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/14/code.py:59:#   - Edge marker colors do not appear as source main colors, so the legend is necessary.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/247ef758/14/code.py:60:#   - The source accent color is shared, but output accent cells become each mover's marker color,\n/