t use at least two marker colors overall and at least two\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D18/2/code.py:36:#   marker colors in the last input frame, so the new rule is visible where the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D18/2/code.py:310:    Key insight: Geometry alone is no longer enough — marker color tells you which distances are legal, so some aligned dots must be ignored even though they look reachable spatially.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/3/code.py:12:# - New marker: the marker color forms exactly two disconnected 1-cell-thick line\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/3/code.py:44:#   removing the true marker color must leave only full rectangular connected components.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/3/code.py:67:# - No new color mapping is introduced. The distinct marker color is structural only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/3/code.py:72:#   enforces this by reserving a unique marker color and scattering rectangular pieces.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/3/code.py:212:    - A unique marker color forms exactly two disconnected line segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b5ca7ac4/D15/2/code.py:186:    - Azure (8) and red (2) framed 5x5 squares are scattered as before.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D8/2/code.py:76:#   Guarantee: marker color is unique; generator rejects piece colors with total count 5.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/16/code.py:204:    assert center_color in MARKER_COLOR_TO_FLIP, \"invalid global flip marker color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/0/code.py:28:#    If the marker color were allowed to tie with payload colors, the task would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/0/code.py:30:#    marker color. The grid still contains all three source behaviors (row, col,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/0/code.py:46:#    The marker color varies across samples and is not red. In many samples red is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D2/0/code.py:58:#    color more pixels than the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D3/2/code.py:33:from a few examples and never hides behind large numeric freedom. The marker colors still directly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D3/2/code.py:59:No hidden color ordering is used. The marker color itself is the square color to visit, exactly as in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/19/code.py:59:#      canvas background avoids marker colors {4,6,7}; hidden marker panels do not overlap the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/19/code.py:74:#    - Background colors deliberately exclude marker colors, so the control panels stand out and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3e6067c3/D14/1/code.py:62:#    The outgoing marker color is not an arbitrary remapping: it literally repeats the inner color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D1/2/code.py:58:#    bg, one marker color, rect_col as border/wildcard, and 1-3 interior colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b5ca7ac4/D14/2/code.py:143:    - Azure squares are processed by increasing input column and copied to the left side; red squares are processed by decreasing input column and copied to the right side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a32d8b75/5/code.py:226:    assert center_color in FLIP_COLOR_TO_MODE, \"invalid flip marker color\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/446ef5d2/D16/2/code.py:76:#    Colors keep the original semantics: bg, one marker color, one rect_col wildcard/\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D9/3/code.py:26:#       - colors: exactly 2 visible motif colors, no dedicated marker color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D9/3/code.py:35:#         - marked border cells use one reserved marker color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D9/3/code.py:55:#     - Only one extra visible concept is introduced: a single marker color on\n/home