ooses three distinct colors and never uses the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/269e22fb/D14/1/code.py:56:#   marker color in the crop.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D11/2/code.py:18:#      marker pixel. Two blue endpoints with the same marker color form one pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D11/2/code.py:31:#      marker colors, and every marker color appears exactly twice.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D11/2/code.py:38:#      That is false now, so grouping must move to \"marker color attached to each blue\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D11/2/code.py:44:#      semantics for unmatched marker colors, so this variant removes blue distractors\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D11/2/code.py:56:#      two blue pixels are the pair\". Repeated marker colors across distant endpoints make\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D11/2/code.py:87:    Pair blue endpoints by nearby marker colors, then extend magenta rays from magenta cells on the chosen diagonals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D11/2/code.py:91:    - Two blue endpoints sharing the same marker color belong to the same pair. Magenta (6) trigger pixels may lie on the interior of those diagonals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D11/2/code.py:94:    - For each marker color, connect its two associated blue endpoints with a blue diagonal segment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D11/2/code.py:98:    - Blue alone no longer determines the pairing; the adjacent marker color is the pairing label, and only the diagonals implied by those labels are active.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/db695cfb/D11/2/code.py:129:        assert len(pts) == 2, \"each marker color must label exactly one blue pair\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D11/1/code.py:50:    Marker bars are thin 4-connected components of the given marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9aaea919/D15/0/code.py:38:#   - `_find_marker_b